Lufus for Debian and Ubuntu
===========================

Lufus is an independent Linux fork of Rufus. Rufus is the first upstream
project credited in the application About window and in the package copyright
file. Lufus and the inherited Rufus work are distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later;
individual inherited files retain their original notices.

Bundled boot components
-----------------------

Pinned boot artifacts and the BCD-SYS scripts are installed with their license
notices and corresponding source. See:

  /usr/share/doc/lufus/copyright
  /usr/share/doc/lufus/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
  /usr/share/lufus/sources/

BCD-SYS is installed from its pinned GPL source scripts. The upstream AppImage
and its duplicate private runtime libraries are not included. Fixed BCD base
hives are generated from BCD-SYS's source templates during the Podman build by
Lufus's native hivex-based importer. A native libhivex editor applies the
Windows To Go internal-disk SAN policy without the removed Perl frontend.

Distribution dependencies
-------------------------

GTK, libadwaita, GLib, libsoup, JSON-GLib and command-line disk/image tools are
normal Debian package dependencies. They are not bundled or relicensed by
Lufus. apt installs them from the target distribution, and their authoritative
notices remain under /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.

Privilege separation
--------------------

Only /usr/libexec/lufus-helper performs privileged disk operations. The polkit
policy authorizes an active local desktop user, while the helper independently
revalidates the selected whole device immediately before destructive access.
